,374,279,897,315,400,76,6199,3,30,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nGiven that $$(m+n+p)(mn+mp+np)=25$$ and that $$m^2(n+p)+n^2(m+p)+p^2(m+n)=4$$ for real numbers $m$, $n$, and $p$, what is the value of $mnp$?","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"24a1e3fd46c4437704209c058c33beaa86e0a724a6d29726440c7c5b06ee5763"},"seconds":9.030943155288696,"seed":763126622159566721,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve for \\(mnp\\), we start with the given equations:\n1. \\((m+n+p)(mn+mp+np) = 25\\)\n2. \\(m^2(n+p) + n^2(m+p) + p^2(m+n) = 4\\)\n\nFirst, let's expand and simplify the second equation. We can rewrite the second equation as follows:\n\\[\nm^2(n+p) + n^2(m+p) + p^2(m+n) = m^2n + m^2p + n^2m + n^2p + p^2m + p^2n\n\\]\nThis can be rearranged as:\n\\[\nm^2n + m^2p + n^2m + n^2p + p^2m + p^2n = (mn + mp + np)(m + n + p) - 3mnp\n\\]\nWe know from the first equation that \\((m+n+p)(mn+mp+np) = 25\\), so we can substitute this into the equation:\n\\[\n(mn + mp + np)(m + n + p) - 3mnp = 4\n\\]\nSubstituting \\((m+n+p)(mn+mp+np) = 25\\) into the equation, we get:\n\\[\n25 - 3mnp = 4\n\\]\nSolving for \\(mnp\\), we get:\n\\[\n25 - 4 = 3mnp \\implies 21 = 3mnp \\implies mnp = 7\n\\]\nThus, the value of \\(mnp\\) is \\(\\boxed{7}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{7}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"algebra:220"}
